Chris Morales wrote:
> What do people think about the ability to discard an artifact.  Is it
> better to have it just discard the artifact, or to replace the
> sacrificed artifact with a new one?

I think the ability to discard an artifact is more flexible and convinient. 
One might not necessarily be looking for an immediate replacement for an 
existing artifact for a myriad of reasons.

Being able to discard an item and reducing the artifact counter seems a 
stratigically better option to me as it affords the player more control over 
the game. Do not increase dependency on the rng without a very compelling 
reason is my philosophy anyway.

Also, increasing anger level of the deity that gifted the artifact (in case 
it was) seems like a natural outcome of discarding artifacts.

